is down into smaller pieces, please let me know.\r\n\r\nThis change introduces the implementation of the library components of the `JobManager`. The `README.md` has a brief introduction to the package structure and what the various packages contain.  It also includes so pointers to running the various tests.  One example:\r\n\r\n```none\r\n$ make test inttest\r\n∅  cmd/cgexec\r\n∅  pkg/adaptation/os\r\n∅  pkg/adaptation/os/ostest\r\n∅  pkg/adaptation/syscall\r\n∅  pkg/adaptation/syscall/syscalltest\r\n✓  pkg/io (17ms) (coverage: 17.0% of statements in ./...)\r\n✓  pkg/command (17ms) (coverage: 15.5% of statements in ./...)\r\n✓  pkg/cgroup/cgroupv1 (17ms) (coverage: 22.8% of statements in ./...)\r\n∅  pkg/cgroup/cgroupv1/cgroupv1test\r\n∅  pkg/config\r\n✓  pkg/jobmanager (27ms) (coverage: 36.8% of statements in ./...)\r\n∅  pkg/jobmanager/jobmanagertest\r\n\r\nDONE 43 tests in 0.261s\r\ngo build -race -o build/cgexec cmd/cgexec/cgexec.go\r\n=== RUN   Test_blkiolimit\r\n--- PASS: Test_blkiolimit (22.09s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/blkiolimit        (cached)\r\n=== RUN   Test_concurrentReads\r\n--- PASS: Test_concurrentReads (40.13s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/concurrentreads   (cached)\r\n=== RUN   Test_cpulimit\r\n--- PASS: Test_cpulimit (20.03s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/cpulimit  (cached)\r\n=== RUN   Test_memorylimit\r\n--- PASS: Test_memorylimit (12.51s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/memorylimit       (cached)\r\n=== RUN   Test_networknamespace\r\n--- PASS: Test_networknamespace (0.01s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/networknamespace  (cached)\r\n=== RUN   Test_jobPidIsOne\r\n--- PASS: Test_jobPidIsOne (0.01s)\r\nPASS\r\nok      github.com/adalton/teleport-exercise/test/job/pidnamespace      (cached)\r\n```\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"adalton","id":751263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MTI2